  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan\u2061x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\u2026,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
